Package: mSigAct2
Title: Mutational Signature Activity Analysis 2 ('mSigAct2')
Version: 1.0.0
Author: Steve Rozen, Alvin Wei Tian Ng, Arnoud Boot, Nanhai Jiang 
Maintainer: Steve Rozen <steverozen@gmail.com>
Description: Analyze the "activities" of mutational signatures in one or more mutational spectra.
    'mSigAct' stands for mutational Signature Activity. mSigAct uses a maximum likelihood approach
    to estimate (conservatively) whether there is evidence that a particular set of mutational 
    signatures is present in a spectrum. It can also determine a *minimal* subset of signatures 
    needed to plausibly reconstruct an observed spectrum. This fork of
    mSigAct2 removes dependencies on ICAMS; these dependencies interferred
    with analysizing data that used new mutation classification schemes.
